lish: one sentence for the subtitle on the gallery card.", "maxLength": 1000, "type": "string"}, "design_systems": {"description": "quickstart only: false when a design system's link is already in hand (it is then read with its own call) or one was declined. Omitted or true, the result lists the design systems (not for a document) and, for slides or a design, attaches the default one's README.", "type": "boolean"}, "edits": {"description": "publish: small changes Claude makes to the file at `file_path` in this same call, instead of editing the file with Edit and publishing after. Use it on a page (add `url` to update an artifact from another conversation) or on one data file of an artifact made from a type (its `url`, with that file as `file_path`). Not allowed with `type_url` or `files`. Each old_str is text copied exactly from the file as it now stands and must occur in it exactly once; new_str takes its place (empty deletes it). The edits apply in order, all or none: the file is published with them and then saved with them on disk, so it stays the source for later changes; on a miss nothing is changed or published, and the result says which edit failed and why.", "items": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"new_str": {"description": "Its replacement; empty deletes old_str.", "type": "string"}, "old_str": {"description": "Text copied exactly from the file; must occur once.", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["old_str", "new_str"], "type": "object"}, "maxItems": 64, "minItems": 1, "type": "array"}, "favicon": {"description": "Deprecated; Claude omits it and uses `icon`.", "maxLength": 32, "minLength": 1, "type": "string"}, "file_path": {"description": "publish: the local page Claude publishes (.html, or .md only when a skill says so). For an Artifact created from an Artifact type, it is one of that Artifact's data files. With `asset: true`, it is the local file Claude uploads. A short, distinctive basename also serves as the title when nothing else gives